  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, poll due Wednesday 18 May 1955. Thirteen Nationalist candidates were nominated for twelve seats, eight for seven in the North Ward and five for five in the South Ward; the Unionist Association nominated none. The independent candidate, Mr. Thomas Campbell, then withdrew, leaving twelve for twelve and no election (Irish News, 5 May 1955, p. 1; Belfast News-Letter, 6 May 1955, p. 10). The withdrawal report of 6 May says there are now '12 Nationalists for 12 seats'. Addresses and occupations printed with the names are left out (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026). Returned unopposed."
